# PART 3: THE AI STUDIO PROMPT

**Copy everything between the two lines below.**

---COPY FROM HERE---

You are a senior product designer and full-stack engineer. Build a complete, polished, production-quality web app called **ShareShelf**, a neighborhood item-sharing platform, for a social-good hackathon. It must be fully working end to end, not a mockup. Write the real, complete code for every screen and flow. No placeholders, no TODOs, no "implement later".

## 1. PRODUCT
Tagline: **Borrow what you need. Share what you have.**
People borrow everyday items (tools, books, electronics, camping gear, event supplies) from neighbors instead of buying things they only need briefly. Core journey: **Discover > Request > Approve > Borrow > Return > Complete.**

## 2. STACK
- React + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, lucide-react icons, React Router (use HashRouter so it works in any host).
- **Supabase** via `@supabase/supabase-js` for auth, database, storage and realtime. All data comes from Supabase. No hard-coded mock data in the UI.
- Read the credentials from `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (also try `process.env` equivalents). If they are missing, show a friendly one-time "Connect Supabase" screen with two fields (Project URL, anon key), save them in localStorage, and continue. Never crash on missing config.
- Load Google Fonts: **Bricolage Grotesque** (headings, weights 600-800) and **Instrument Sans** (body and UI, 400-600).
- Organize code into clean files: `lib/supabase.ts`, `lib/api.ts` (all queries), `hooks/`, `components/`, `pages/`. Keep components readable and well named.

## 3. DATABASE (already created, use exactly these names)
- `profiles(id, full_name, neighborhood)`
- `items(id, owner_id, name, description, category, condition, image_url, neighborhood, is_available, rules, replacement_value, is_demo, created_at)`
- `borrow_requests(id, item_id, borrower_id, owner_id, start_date, end_date, message, status, is_demo, created_at, updated_at)` with status in: `pending, approved, rejected, active, return_requested, completed, cancelled`
- `item_wants(id, requester_id, title, description, category, neighborhood, needed_by, status, is_demo, created_at)`
- `want_responses(id, want_id, responder_id, message, created_at)`
- `notifications(id, user_id, message, is_read, created_at)`
- Views: `item_busy_dates(item_id, start_date, end_date, status)` (reserved date ranges, readable by everyone) and `community_impact(items_listed, completed_exchanges, borrowed_now, money_saved, items_reused, demo_items)`.
- Storage bucket `item-images` (public) for uploaded item photos.
- Notifications are created automatically by database triggers. Do NOT insert them from the client. The database also rejects overlapping reserved loans and invalid status changes, so catch those errors and show a clear human message ("Those dates are already reserved for this item.").
- Categories: Tools, Electronics, Education, Household, Outdoor, Events, Sports, Other. Conditions: Like new, Good, Fair.

## 4. BRAND AND VISUAL SYSTEM (follow exactly)
**Feeling:** premium, friendly, trustworthy social-impact startup that could launch publicly. Definitely not a generic ecommerce template.

**Colors (define as CSS variables and Tailwind theme colors):**
forest `#234B35`, deep-forest `#173325`, sage `#DCE8DA`, sage-mist `#EEF3EA`, cream `#F8F7F2` (page background), white `#FFFFFF` (cards), charcoal `#202820` (text), muted `#7A827B`, lime `#B6D67A` (highlights; always pair with forest text), amber `#E8B84B` on `#FBF1D3` (pending), clay `#B3402F` on `#F6DDD7` (rejected/errors). Hairline borders `#E3E7DE`.

**Type:** Bricolage Grotesque for headings (tight letter-spacing, weight 700-800), Instrument Sans for everything else. Sentence case everywhere. No all-caps labels, no tracked-out eyebrow text.

**Shape:** cards 20px radius, buttons and chips fully rounded, inputs 12px. Soft shadow `0 6px 20px rgba(35,75,53,.07)`. Generous whitespace. No heavy gradients. Primary button: forest with white text, deep-forest on hover. Secondary: white with border. Destructive: clay outline.

**Logo:** use this SVG inline as a `Logo` component next to the wordmark "ShareShelf" (Bricolage Grotesque 800, forest):
```
<svg viewBox="0 0 48 48"><rect width="48" height="48" rx="14" fill="#234B35"/><rect x="10" y="21" width="20" height="4" rx="2" fill="#DCE8DA"/><rect x="14" y="11" width="8" height="10" rx="3" fill="#B6D67A"/><rect x="18" y="35" width="20" height="4" rx="2" fill="#DCE8DA"/><rect x="28" y="25" width="8" height="10" rx="3" fill="#B6D67A"/></svg>
```
Also set it as the favicon.

**Signature element, used only in two places:** the **shelf line**, a 6px rounded forest bar. (1) In the hero, four item cards rest on it, slightly staggered. (2) In empty states, a single lone item icon sits on a short shelf line.

**Item images:** if `image_url` is empty or fails to load, show a designed fallback tile: sage-mist background with a large lucide icon matched to the category (Wrench for Tools, Plug for Electronics, BookOpen for Education, Home for Household, Tent for Outdoor, PartyPopper for Events, Trophy for Sports, Package for Other), in forest at 60% opacity. Never show a broken image icon. Use `object-cover` with consistent aspect ratio (4:3) for every card.

**Motion:** minimal. Only respond to user actions: modal and drawer open/close (150-200ms), toast slide-in, button press, status badge change. No scroll-triggered animations. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

**Voice:** warm, plain, neighborly. Buttons are verbs ("Request to borrow", "Approve", "Confirm return", "Share an item"). Errors say what happened and how to fix it. Empty states invite an action.

## 5. NAVIGATION (must be effortless)
**Desktop (>=1024px):** sticky top bar on cream with a bottom hairline. Left: logo + wordmark. Center: **Discover, Wanted board, My activity, Impact** (active item gets a sage pill). Right: a **Share an item** primary button, a notification bell with unread count badge and dropdown panel, and an avatar menu (name, neighborhood, "Switch demo user" if signed in as a demo account, Sign out).
**Mobile (<1024px):** slim top bar with logo on the left, bell and avatar on the right. A **fixed bottom tab bar** with 5 items: Discover, Wanted, a raised center **+ Share** button (forest circle), My activity, Impact. Touch targets at least 44px. My activity shows a small lime badge with the number of items needing the user's action.
Routes: `/` Discover, `/wanted`, `/activity`, `/impact`, `/item/:id` (opens as modal over Discover on desktop, full page on mobile), `/auth`.
Browsing (Discover, Wanted, Impact, item details) works **without** signing in. Any action that needs an account (request, share, respond, activity) opens a friendly sign-in modal, then continues where the user left off.

## 6. AUTH
Supabase email + password. Sign-in modal and `/auth` page: two-panel layout on desktop (left: forest panel with the logo, tagline and the shelf-line illustration; right: form), single column on mobile. Tabs for **Sign in** and **Create account** (full name, neighborhood, email, password). Inline validation and friendly errors.
Add a clearly labeled **"Prototype demo"** box with two buttons that sign in instantly: **Continue as Alex Morgan (item owner)** with `alex@shareshelf.demo` and **Continue as Jordan Lee (borrower)** with `jordan@shareshelf.demo`, both with password `ShareShelf!2026`. The avatar menu has **Switch to Jordan / Switch to Alex** for these accounts so judges can demo both sides quickly. Show a subtle "Prototype demo" tag near the logo.

## 7. SCREENS

### Discover (`/`)
- **Hero** on cream: headline "Good things are better when shared." (large Bricolage Grotesque), supporting text "Borrow everyday essentials from your community, save money, and give useful things a second life.", buttons **Explore items** (scrolls to the grid) and **Share an item**. Below the buttons a small sage pill: "Your neighborhood is full of things worth sharing." On the right, four real item cards (pulled from Supabase) resting on the forest shelf line. Do NOT show invented user counts or statistics.
- **Search bar** (large, rounded, search icon, clear button; live filtering by name, description, category, neighborhood) and a **category chip row** (All items + 8 categories; horizontal scroll on mobile). Also a neighborhood dropdown and a "Available now" toggle. Show a result count.
- **Item cards** in a responsive grid (1/2/3/4 columns): 4:3 image, availability badge (lime "Available", sage "On loan" when it has a reserved range covering today, gray "Unavailable"), name, category, condition, neighborhood, owner name with small avatar initials, a **FREE** label, and a View details button. The whole card is clickable.
- Loading: skeleton cards. Empty: shelf-line empty state "Nothing matches yet" with buttons "Clear filters" and "Ask your neighbors" (goes to Wanted board).

### Item details
Large image, name, category, condition, description, owner card (avatar, name, neighborhood), borrowing rules, cost FREE, and a **reserved dates** strip from `item_busy_dates` ("Reserved 12 Dec - 14 Dec"). A "How borrowing works" mini-explainer: Request, Owner approves, Pick up and return. The primary button **Request to borrow** opens the request form inside the same panel:
- Start date, return date (native date inputs, min = today). Validate: return not before start, dates not in the past, no overlap with reserved ranges (show inline: "Those dates overlap a reserved loan. Try another range."), message to the owner (optional, 300 chars with counter).
- On submit, insert into `borrow_requests` with status `pending` and `owner_id` from the item. Show a success toast "Request sent to Alex" and navigate to My activity > My requests.
- If the viewer is the owner, show "This is your item" with Edit and Remove buttons instead. If the item is unavailable, disable the request button with an explanation.

### My activity (`/activity`)
Requires sign-in. Header: "Hi, {first name}" and a one-line summary ("2 things need your attention"). A horizontally scrollable tab bar with counts: **My items, Incoming requests, Items I'm borrowing, My requests, Active loans, Completed exchanges**. Default to the tab with the most urgent action.
Each request is a card with: item thumbnail and name, the other person, dates, message, a **progress stepper** (Requested > Approved > Picked up > Returned > Complete) with the current step highlighted in forest and finished steps in lime, a status badge, and action buttons based on role and status:
- Owner, `pending`: **Approve** (forest) and **Reject** (clay outline).
- Borrower, `pending` or `approved`: **Cancel request**.
- Borrower, `approved`: **I picked it up** (status > `active`).
- Borrower, `active`: **Request return confirmation** (status > `return_requested`).
- Owner, `return_requested`: **Confirm item returned** (status > `completed`).
Every action updates Supabase, shows a toast, and updates the UI instantly (optimistic update with rollback on error). If Approve fails because of a date clash, show the friendly message.
**My items** tab: list of the user's items with availability toggle, **Edit** and **Remove** (with a confirmation dialog; block removal while a loan is approved or active, with a clear reason). Include an **Add item** button.
Each tab has a helpful empty state with a next step.

### Share an item (modal on desktop, full-screen sheet on mobile; also used for Edit)
Fields: item name, description, category, condition, **photo upload** to the `item-images` bucket (drag and drop on desktop, camera/gallery on mobile, preview and remove) with an optional image URL alternative, neighborhood, availability, borrowing instructions, and estimated replacement value in USD (helper text: "Used to estimate how much the community saves"). Validate every field with inline messages. On save, show a success toast and the new item appears in Discover immediately.

### Wanted board (`/wanted`)
Headline "Can't find it? Ask your neighbors." A **Request an item** button opens a form (item needed, description, category, neighborhood, date needed). Show open requests as cards: title, description, category, neighborhood, "Needed by" date, requester, response count, and a **Respond** button. Respond opens a panel listing existing responses and a message box ("I have one you can borrow"). The requester can mark their request **fulfilled** or delete it. Filter by category. Empty state invites the first request.

### Impact (`/impact`)
Read from the `community_impact` view only. Five large number cards: **Items listed, Completed exchanges, Borrowed right now, Estimated money saved ($), Items reused**. Add a simple bar chart (inline SVG or CSS bars) of items by category computed from `items`. Include a "How we calculate this" card: money saved is the sum of the estimated replacement value of items in completed exchanges; items reused counts distinct items borrowed and returned. Include a clear note: "Includes {demo_items} demonstration items. Figures are estimates, not real-world results." Numbers update live. Never present fabricated statistics.

### Notifications
Bell dropdown (desktop) and full-screen list (mobile) listing recent notifications from the `notifications` table with relative times, unread highlight, and a "Mark all as read" action. New notifications arrive live and also pop up as a toast.

## 8. REALTIME
Subscribe with Supabase realtime to `borrow_requests`, `notifications`, `items` and `item_wants`, so when Alex approves a request, Jordan's screen updates without refreshing. Clean up subscriptions on unmount.

## 9. UX AND QUALITY BAR
- Every button and link does something real. No decorative controls.
